;; FOUND by the ESH-0101 guard coverage gate. Ledger: SW-87.
;; NATIVE ONLY (jit, aot-o0, aot-o2). Both VM axes accept this and answer
;; correctly, so it is also a native-vs-VM divergence.
;;
;; R7RS derives `guard` through `(let ((var condition)) ...)`, and a let-bound
;; variable is assignable, so `set!` on the guard variable inside a clause is
;; legal. Native codegen binds the guard variable to an SSA VALUE rather than
;; to an alloca, so the assignment is rejected outright:
;;
;;   ERROR: set!: variable 'e' is not mutable
;;          (not an alloca, global, or capture pointer)
;;
;; LOUD, not silent — it fails to compile rather than answering wrongly.
;;
;; want: (mutated orig)
(display (guard (e (#t (set! e (list 'mutated e)) e)) (raise 'orig)))
(newline)
